Section 11  License Verification Mechanism


The Licensed Work may include license verification
mechanisms for the purposes of:

(a) verifying authorization status;

(b) preventing unauthorized Production Use;

(c) protecting the legitimate rights and interests of
    the Licensor.


Such mechanisms may process limited information
necessary for license verification, including:

(a) publicly accessible deployment addresses;

(b) domain names or access addresses associated with
    the deployment environment;

(c) software version information;

(d) license verification results;

(e) verification timestamps.


The Licensor shall use such information only for:

(a) license management;

(b) authorization verification;

(c) compliance notification;

(d) enforcement of this License.


The license verification mechanism shall not be used
for collecting user business data unrelated to license
verification.


