Section 12  Unauthorized Mode


If the Licensor determines that the Licensed Work is
being used for Production Use without a valid commercial
license, the Licensed Work may enter an unauthorized
mode.


In unauthorized mode, the Licensed Work may:

(a) display authorization status notices;

(b) display license reminder messages;

(c) display authorization status watermarks;

(d) limit certain non-essential functions;

(e) request completion of authorization verification.


The purpose of unauthorized mode is to notify users of
authorization status and facilitate compliance with this
License.


The Licensor shall provide reasonable methods for users
who believe the authorization status is incorrect to
submit proof of authorization and request verification.


Upon successful verification or completion of licensing
requirements, authorized use may be restored.


